      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] There appears to be a mismatch between this logic and the `REAL_IMAGE_PROPS` in the devicetree overlay.\n\nFor `FINGERPRINT_CAPTURE_TYPE_SIMPLE_IMAGE`, `apply_image_offset` will be `true`, so `offset` will be 400. Since `frame-size` is 25600, `offset + frame_size` equals 26000. If the caller allocates based on the reported `frame-size` (25600), this check will return `-EINVAL`, effectively breaking simple image acquisition.\n\nIf `SIMPLE_IMAGE` should NOT have an offset, it should be added to the exclusion list here, or `image-data-offset-bytes` should remain 0 in `REAL_IMAGE_PROPS`.",
      "revId": "add45d94dea0a62e23117d8540da21be405e212e",
