      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Regarding the source pointer: if `config-\u003eimage_buffer` was loaded with a full raw frame (e.g., via `z_impl_fingerprint_load_image`), then `config-\u003eimage_buffer` begins with the 400-byte header.\n\nWhen `offset` is 400 (as for `SIMPLE_IMAGE`), this `memcpy` will copy the *header* into the destination buffer (at `image_buf + 400`) instead of the pixel data. Should the source also be shifted by `offset`?\n\n```c\nmemcpy(image_buf + offset, config-\u003eimage_buffer + offset, frame_size);\n```",
      "revId": "add45d94dea0a62e23117d8540da21be405e212e",
