      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] The bounds check correctly prevents out-of-bounds writes. However, there appears to be a contradiction between the driver logic and the devicetree configuration in the simulator overlay.\n\nFor capture types using `REAL_IMAGE_PROPS` (e.g., `SIMPLE_IMAGE`), the `frame-size` is 25600 and `image-data-offset-bytes` is now 400. In `fp_simulator_acquire_image`, `apply_image_offset` will be `true` for these modes, setting `offset` to 400. Consequently, `offset + frame_size` (26000) will exceed `image_buf_size` if the caller allocates based on the provided `frame_size` (25600), causing this check to return `-EINVAL`.\n\nIf these modes are intended to have an offset, `frame-size` in the overlay should be increased to 26000. If they are NOT intended to have an offset (as suggested in your previous response), then `image-data-offset-bytes` should remain 0 in `REAL_IMAGE_PROPS`, or these capture types should be added to the exclusion list in the driver code.",
      "revId": "add45d94dea0a62e23117d8540da21be405e212e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
